(1) A declaration signed by hand by the person referred to in § 28(1) point 1 of the Zahlungsdiensteaufsichtsgesetz, on the form in Annex 4 to this Regulation, must be enclosed with the notification of intention under § 28(1) point 1 of the Zahlungsdiensteaufsichtsgesetz, in which the person must state whether
1. criminal proceedings are being conducted against the person, or criminal proceedings for a serious or less serious criminal offence were conducted against the person at an earlier time;
2. in connection with an entrepreneurial or other professional activity, administrative offence proceedings or comparable proceedings under another legal system are being conducted against the person or have been concluded with a conviction or other sanction;
3. insolvency proceedings, proceedings for a statutory declaration in lieu of an oath or comparable proceedings are being conducted, or were conducted at an earlier time, against the person or against an undertaking managed by the person;
4. a supervisory authority has initiated a review of reliability or suitability under trade law or supervisory proceedings for the adoption of measures, or such proceedings have already been concluded with a sanction;
5. a public body has refused, cancelled, withdrawn, revoked or deleted an authorisation, membership or registration in the name of the person or of an undertaking or business managed by the person, or has otherwise prohibited the exercise of a profession, the operation of a business or the representation or management of business affairs, or corresponding proceedings are being conducted.
The proceedings and sanctions stated must be explained. Officially certified copies of the judgments, decisions, other sanctions or other documents concluding the proceedings must be enclosed. In the information under sentence 1 point 1, criminal proceedings may be disregarded that were discontinued for lack of sufficient suspicion of an offence or because of a procedural bar, or that ended in an acquittal, or in which an entry made in the Bundeszentralregister has been removed or expunged, or that need not be stated under § 53 of the Bundeszentralregistergesetz. The same applies to criminal proceedings that were not concluded by a German criminal investigation authority or by a German court. Proceedings discontinued under §§ 153 and 153a of the Strafprozessordnung must be stated. Entries that must be expunged from the Gewerbezentralregister under § 153 of the Gewerbeordnung need not be mentioned. In the information under sentence 1 points 2, 4 and 5, proceedings may be disregarded that were concluded with a conviction, sanction or other decision more than five years before the beginning of the year in which the notification is submitted.

(2) As further evidence of reliability and as evidence of adequate theoretical and practical knowledge and skills for providing payment services, a complete curriculum vitae of the person concerned, signed by hand, must be enclosed with the notification of intention under § 28(1) point 1 of the Zahlungsdiensteaufsichtsgesetz; it must contain the full name including all first names, the name at birth, the date of birth, the place of birth, the country of birth, the principal residence, the nationality, the professional qualifications including the degrees obtained, further training, and the professional experience, which must be set out in chronological order beginning with the profession currently exercised. For the professional experience, the name and registered office of all undertakings for which the person works or worked, the nature and duration of the activity, including secondary activities but excluding honorary activities, the person's power of representation, the person's internal decision-making powers and the business areas reporting to the person within the undertaking must be stated. The form in Annex 5 to this Regulation must be used to state the secondary activities. The holding of a direct interest of at least 25 per cent of the shares in the capital of an undertaking must be stated. The form in Annex 6 to this Regulation must be used to state the direct holdings.

(3) The persons named in the notification of intention under § 28(1) point 1 of the Zahlungsdiensteaufsichtsgesetz must submit to the Bundesanstalt a certificate of good conduct for submission to an authority under § 30(5) or § 30b of the Bundeszentralregistergesetz. At the time the notification under § 28(1) point 1 of the Zahlungsdiensteaufsichtsgesetz is made, the certificate of good conduct must not be older than three months. The date of issue of the certificate of good conduct is decisive. § 5c(3) to (5) of the Anzeigenverordnung apply accordingly.

(4) The persons named in the notification of intention under § 28(1) point 1 of the Zahlungsdiensteaufsichtsgesetz must apply to the Bundesamt für Justiz for an extract from the Gewerbezentralregister under § 150(5) of the Gewerbeordnung for submission to the Bundesanstalt. Sentence 1 does not apply if the person has neither had a residence in the Federal Republic of Germany in the last ten years nor carried on a professional activity in the Federal Republic of Germany in the last ten years. Where the Bundesanstalt already holds an extract from the Gewerbezentralregister under § 150(5) of the Gewerbeordnung that was applied for not more than twelve months ago, no new application to the Bundesamt für Justiz is required.

(5) The employment contract, the planned start date and the planned duration of the mandate, a description of the essential duties and responsibilities and other information relevant to the assessment of reliability must be enclosed with the notification.

(6) At the request of the Bundesanstalt, further information must be provided and documents submitted, in particular employment references documenting the activities stated in the curriculum vitae.

