(1) Any person who, as a trader, offers the conclusion of consumer loans within the meaning of § 491 of the Bürgerliches Gesetzbuch must state as the price the total cost of the consumer loan to the consumer, calculated in accordance with subsections (2) to (6) and (8) and expressed as an annual percentage of the net loan amount, including, where applicable, the costs under subsection (3) sentence 2 point 2, and must designate it as the annual percentage rate of charge.

(2) The annual percentage rate of charge must be calculated using the mathematical formula set out in the Annex and in accordance with the procedures on which the Annex is based. The annual percentage rate of charge is calculated on the assumption that the consumer loan agreement remains valid for the period agreed and that the lender and the consumer fulfil their obligations under the terms and by the dates laid down in the consumer loan agreement.

(3) The calculation of the annual percentage rate of charge must include, as the total cost, the interest payable by the consumer and all other costs that the consumer must pay in connection with the consumer loan agreement and that are known to the lender. The other costs under sentence 1 include:
1. costs of arranging the consumer loan;
2. costs of opening and maintaining a specific account, costs of using a means of payment with which both transactions on that account can be carried out and consumer loan amounts can be drawn down, and other costs of payment transactions, where the opening or maintenance of an account is a condition for the consumer loan being granted at all or on the terms provided for in the contract;
3. costs of property valuation, where such a valuation is necessary for the consumer loan to be granted.

(4) The following must not be included in the calculation of the total cost:
1. costs payable by the consumer for non-compliance with any of the consumer's obligations under the consumer loan agreement;
2. costs of insurance and of other additional services that are not a condition for the consumer loan being granted at all or on the terms provided for in the contract;
3. costs, other than the purchase price, payable by the consumer on the purchase of goods or services, irrespective of whether the transaction is paid in cash or by consumer loan;
4. fees for the registration of the transfer of ownership or of the transfer of a right equivalent to real property in the land register;
5. notarial fees.

(5) Where a change in the interest rate or in other costs to be included in the calculation of the annual percentage rate of charge is reserved and cannot be quantified at the time the annual percentage rate of charge is calculated, the calculation is made on the assumption that the borrowing rate and the other costs remain fixed in relation to their initial level and apply until the end of the consumer loan agreement.

(6) Where the assumptions set out in the Annex apply, they must be taken into account in calculating the annual percentage rate of charge.

(7) Where the conclusion of a contract for an ancillary service, in particular an insurance contract or a membership in general, is compulsory in order for the consumer loan to be granted at all or on the terms provided for in the contract, and the costs of the ancillary service cannot be determined in advance, attention must be drawn in a clear, unambiguous and prominent manner to
1. the fact that there is an obligation to conclude the contract for the ancillary service, and
2. the annual percentage rate of charge of the consumer loan.

(8) For building savings loans, the annual percentage rate of charge must be calculated on the assumption that the contractual minimum savings balance has been saved at the time the consumer loan is paid out. In case of doubt, only the part of the arrangement fee attributable to the consumer loan portion of the building savings contract amount is to be taken into account. For consumer loans that serve the advance or interim financing of benefits of a Bausparkasse under building savings contracts and whose price-determining factors cannot be changed until allocation, the term must be based on the allocation periods resulting from the target rating figure for building savings contracts of the same kind. For building savings contracts financed in advance or on an interim basis under sentence 3, the annual percentage rate of charge for the total term must be stated for the overall product consisting of the advance or interim financing loan and the building savings contract.
